				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule — Notification delegation completion and provider lifecycle symmetry\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to b08029a4, integrating final notification consolidation across Mountain and Vine.\n\nMountain eliminates all local `super::Notification::*` dispatch logic by delegating directly to `::Vine::Server::Notification::*`. The `MountainVinegRPCService` is reduced to a pure routing table, retaining only Mountain-specific utilities (`Support`, `OutputChannelCoalesce`, `TerminalEnvCollection`).\n\nVine inlines trivial unregistration atoms (`UnregisterFileSystemProvider`, `UnregisterUriHandler`) that only performed single-step delegation, retaining `UnregisterScmProvider` which contains DJB-31 handle recomputation and Sky event relay logic. This consolidates the unregistration surface to expose only atoms with multi-step orchestration needs.\n\nMountain is now a pure composition layer with all Cocoon→Mountain IPC contracts defined canonically in Vine. The provider lifecycle is fully symmetrical with clean disposal pathways, and redundant wrapper modules have been eliminated.",
			"SHA": "6b993bb51fed4ea0a813200d24ed67fa609dc2c3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:03:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule — Notification delegation completion and provider lifecycle symmetry\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to 536326f2, integrating updates across Cache, Mountain, and Vine.\n\nCache reformats documentation comments in Library.rs for improved readability.\n\nMountain completes the systematic decomposition of the gRPC notification surface by delegating all remaining handlers to the Vine crate. Convert CocoonService and MountainService trait imports to use canonical definitions from ::Vine::Generated, eliminating local re-exports. Server-side notification modules (UpdateScmGroup, WebviewLifecycle, RelayToSky, provider unregistration) are now thin shims forwarding to Vine::Server::Notification. Client-side Shared module and stub implementations are reduced to empty pass-throughs.\n\nVine implements the symmetrical provider unregistration surface — UnregisterRemoteAuthorityResolver, UnregisterScmProvider, UnregisterTaskProvider, and UnregisterUriHandler — all integrating with the central UnregisterByHandle utility. Add WebviewLifecycle notification to canonicalize Cocoon's positional arrays into named-key objects before emitting to Sky renderer channels. Implement UpdateScmGroup notification with SCM marker persistence via VineHost::UpdateScmGroupMarkers for boot-time replay. Enhance UnregisterFileSystemProvider with scheme logging for diagnostic observability.\n\nMountain is now a pure composition layer with all Cocoon→Mountain IPC delegated to the shared Vine crate. The provider lifecycle is fully symmetrical with clean disposal pathways, and SCM/webview state persists across page reloads.",
			"SHA": "efe952b0cc9cc6e1b5f0801256070857254c5256"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T13:56:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule — Grove reformat, Vine terminal/SCM/language registry\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to 079fec72, integrating updates across Grove and Vine.\n\nGrove reformats `Source/Transport/Strategy.rs` — splits `connect`, `send`, `close` method chains onto separate lines across gRPC, IPC, WASM, and WebSocket variants to match organization formatting standards.\n\nVine expands the `VineHost` trait surface: implements `TerminalLifecycle` and `WindowCreateTerminal` to bridge Cocoon PTY requests with native providers, adds `RegisterScmProvider`/`RegisterScmResourceGroup` for SCM viewlet integration, and introduces a centralized `RegisterLanguageProvider` dispatcher that normalizes 46+ wire method names to standardized `TypeName` identifiers before routing to the embedder registry.\n\nExtension-driven terminal sessions, SCM provider registration, and full VS Code language intelligence features are now supported via the gRPC notification surface.",
			"SHA": "30ef9a58b33fa9dd39f7c54cceb5675e33de1de3"
		},
